                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2872666,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "With data like this, acoustic engineers have been able to build up what we call noise maps maps of the sound environment. But actually, these aren't a lot of use. What they do show is that the highest noise levels are generally on roads. Well, that's not really very surprising. But there's quite a lot going on that these maps don't show, because they can't capture the complex way that sound varies over time.",
