          },
          {
            "id": 2872917,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "It's also known that noise can lead to a rise in levels of stress, due to physical changes in the body affecting the composition of the blood. And there are other problems as well for instance, if schoolchildren don't have a quiet place to study, their work will suffer. Now one problem with decibel measurement is that it doesn't differentiate between different types of noise. Some types of sounds that most people would probably think of as nice and relaxing might well score quite highly in decibel levels. Think of the sound made by a fountain in a town square, for example.",
